<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"FONT-FAMILY: '=B8=BC=C0=BA =B0=ED=B5=
=F1'; FONT-SIZE: 10pt" lang=3D"EN-US">In order to set up LCF lane QTA, plea=
se consider the below factors.</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; MARGIN-LEFT: 38pt; mso-para-margin-left: 0g=
d; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1" class=3D"MsoListParagraph">
<span style=3D"FONT-FAMILY: '=B8=BC=C0=BA =B0=ED=B5=F1'; FONT-SIZE: 10pt" l=
ang=3D"EN-US"><span style=3D"mso-list: Ignore">-<span style=3D"FONT: 7pt 'T=
imes New Roman'">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><span style=3D"FONT-FAMILY: '=B8=BC=C0=BA =B0=ED=B5=F1=
'; FONT-SIZE: 10pt" lang=3D"EN-US">Due to the Lane priority of LCF lane on =
ALPS system, almost T/S volume=A1=AFs performance on LCF lane will be trans=
ferred to that of other connected lanes to/from LCF.</span></p>
<p style=3D"MARGIN-LEFT: 38pt; mso-para-margin-left: 0gd" class=3D"MsoListP=
aragraph">
<span style=3D"FONT-FAMILY: '=B8=BC=C0=BA =B0=ED=B5=F1'; FONT-SIZE: 10pt" l=
ang=3D"EN-US">So, for LCF lane=A1=AFs QTA, only genuine LCF direct service =
performance from/to Direct calling ports on LCF should be considered.
</span></p>
<p style=3D"TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; MARGIN-LEFT: 38pt; mso-para-margin-left: 0g=
d; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1" class=3D"MsoListParagraph">
<span style=3D"FONT-FAMILY: '=B8=BC=C0=BA =B0=ED=B5=F1'; FONT-SIZE: 10pt" l=
ang=3D"EN-US"><span style=3D"mso-list: Ignore">-<span style=3D"FONT: 7pt 'T=
imes New Roman'">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><span style=3D"FONT-FAMILY: '=B8=BC=C0=BA =B0=ED=B5=F1=
'; FONT-SIZE: 10pt" lang=3D"EN-US">Based on LCF lane=A1=AFs BSA Commitment =
Ratio (IAS&#43;IAS T/S : 62%, &nbsp;T/S of TPS/AES : 38%), the available sp=
ace for pure IAS volume is 62%.</span></p>
<p style=3D"MARGIN-LEFT: 38pt; mso-para-margin-left: 0gd" class=3D"MsoListP=
aragraph">
<span style=3D"FONT-FAMILY: '=B8=BC=C0=BA =B0=ED=B5=F1'; FONT-SIZE: 10pt" l=
ang=3D"EN-US">Under 62% BSA, if there is higher CMPB of regular IAS T/S vol=
ume, 62% BSA must be firstly allocated to IAS T/S lane.&nbsp;
</span></p>
<p style=3D"MARGIN-LEFT: 38pt; mso-para-margin-left: 0gd" class=3D"MsoListP=
aragraph">
<span style=3D"FONT-FAMILY: '=B8=BC=C0=BA =B0=ED=B5=F1'; FONT-SIZE: 10pt" l=
ang=3D"EN-US">After that, finally, the rest of BSA on LCF lane is for the p=
ure LCF direct service volume to INMAA.</span></p>
<p style=3D"TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; MARGIN-LEFT: 38pt; mso-para-margin-left: 0g=
d; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1" class=3D"MsoListParagraph">
<span style=3D"FONT-FAMILY: '=B8=BC=C0=BA =B0=ED=B5=F1'; FONT-SIZE: 10pt" l=
ang=3D"EN-US"><span style=3D"mso-list: Ignore">-<span style=3D"FONT: 7pt 'T=
imes New Roman'">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><span style=3D"FONT-FAMILY: '=B8=BC=C0=BA =B0=ED=B5=F1=
'; FONT-SIZE: 10pt" lang=3D"EN-US">Considering above factors, please give u=
s your QTA idea for LCF(W/B)</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span style=3D"FONT-FAMILY: '=B8=BC=C0=BA =B0=ED=B5=
